The 'Data Repair' engine in the Admin System Settings (/admin/settings) provides managed, three-phase workflows for resolving organizational data inconsistencies.
1. Scope: The suite targets 'Orphaned Org KPI Propagations' (KPIs stuck at 'kra_set' despite available org data) and 'Stepped-Back Siblings' (2026+ multi-month KPIs stuck at 'kra_set' when their terminal sibling is already 'approved').
2. Workflow: Both tools follow a Scan → Select → Repair lifecycle. The 'Scan' phase provides a read-only preview of repairable records with status reasons, scoped by cascading organizational filters (Division -> Business Unit -> Department). 'Repair' is targeted to user-selected IDs and gated by a 'ConfirmDestructiveDialog'.
3. Recovery Logic: Sibling repair re-runs percolation and supports three distinct recovery paths:
   - Same-Year: Inherits data from an approved terminal sibling in the same year.
   - Cross-Year: Correctly resolves cycles spanning year boundaries (e.g., matching a January 2026 sibling to a December 2025 terminal).
   - Audit-Log Self-Recovery: Reconstructs 'review_submissions' entries by merging historical data from audit logs.
   All sibling repairs advance status to 'approved', set 'final_score' to the resolved value, and use 'locked' as the 'kpi_status' in submission records.
4. Validation ('200 checks'): After execution, the engine runs automated verification queries (limited to 200 records each) to confirm status advancement and submission existence, reporting results in a dedicated dashboard.
5. Performance & Scaling: To handle high-volume datasets (1,500+ records) and prevent 504 timeouts, the engine utilizes batch pre-fetching into memory structures (Sets and Maps) and fetches database records in 500-row batches to bypass the 1000-row default limit.
6. Reporting: Generates multi-sheet Excel reports (Summary, Details, Errors) for both Scan and Repair phases.
7. Bucket-Specific Repair Cards: The Data Repair tab now hosts dedicated cards for (a) Bucket B/C "Repair Orphaned Propagations" (legacy edge function), (b) Bucket F "Repair Propagation Failures" (resets OKV.status='propagated' → 'draft' when zero employees advanced — v2.65.9), (c) Bucket K "Repair Late-Joiner Org KPIs" (v2.66.3 — invokes 'backfill_late_joiner_org_kpis(p_dry_run)' RPC; admin-only; dry-run scan + confirmed apply uses identical scope-resolution logic as the live trigger), and (d) "Reconcile Org KPI Inheritance" (v2.66.6 — invokes 'reconcile_org_kpi_inheritance(p_dry_run)' RPC; finds existing employee KPIs that have an Org-level sibling with the same signature but aren't yet Org-level themselves and bulk-promotes them; audit action 'ORG_KPI_INHERITANCE_RECONCILED'; the existing autopull trigger then fills any propagated values for promoted rows).
